{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":139371,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c45b8ac5-04c5-566b-bdbc-0406d58cb943","total_cost_usd":0.8120299999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9317,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":12402,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9317,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12402,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9317,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9317},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5490,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.00557,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12402,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9317,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.80646,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:dependence-c-reviewer-fable-11\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:07367ef4946f4b4def3f\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Every k1 identifier (u01–u12) and every k2 identifier appears exactly once across the 12 staged rows, so no source item enters the procedure more than once.\", \"observed_value\": \"12 rows, 12 distinct k1 codes, 12 distinct k2 codes\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 2, \"quoted_text\": \"u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 13, \"quoted_text\": \"u12,v06,t12,12.0,12.0\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The applied procedure is an unpaired, row-independent rank test over the two disjoint samples; with unique units per row this matches the stated data structure.\", \"observed_value\": \"mannwhitneyu, statistic=60.5, p=0.524\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"result = st.mannwhitneyu(left, right)\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] MannwhitneyuResult(statistic=np.float64(60.5), pvalue=np.float64(0.5243792697676437))\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Strongest candidate for the issue: both samples are extracted from the same staged rows, which could superficially suggest shared structure; however the task declares the row pairing a storage convention only and no identifier repeats, so no repeated-unit entry occurs.\", \"observed_value\": \"no duplicated k1 or k2 code\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 6, \"end_line\": 7, \"quoted_text\": \"left = [float(row[\\\"a\\\"]) for row in staged]\\nright = [float(row[\\\"b\\\"]) for row in staged]\"}, {\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"The row pairing is a storage convention only; there is no matching, pairing, block, or other relationship between the `k1` item and the `k2` item in that row.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to falsify the negative verdict by scanning all 12 rows for any repeated k1 code, repeated k2 code, or duplicated full row, and by checking whether the reported statistic implies an inflated sample count. All identifiers are distinct, and a Mann-Whitney U of 60.5 with p=0.524 is consistent with 12-vs-12 samples. No route to demonstrating repeated unit entry survived.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:15afc5ae0e707246f8c0\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"The selected report's independent-samples t-test result (df=46.0) was computed over a staged row sequence in which every source item's row appears exactly twice (e.g., k1=u01 on two consecutive rows), so each independent unit enters the row-independent procedure twice and the effective sample size is doubled from 12 to 24 per collection.\", \"root_cause\": \"The workflow feeds the complete staged sequence, containing an exact second entry for every unit identifier, into scipy.stats.ttest_ind, which treats each row as an independent observation; the duplicated entries of the same k1/k2 source items are therefore counted as additional independent observations, inflating degrees of freedom from 22 to 46.\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Each unit's row appears exactly twice in the staged data; the first duplicated pair shows k1=u01 entered twice with identical measurements, and the pattern repeats through u12/v06.\", \"observed_value\": \"24 rows = 12 units × 2 identical entries each\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 3, \"quoted_text\": \"u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0\\nu01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 24, \"end_line\": 25, \"quoted_text\": \"u12,v06,t12,12.0,12.0\\nu12,v06,t12,12.0,12.0\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The task defines k1 and k2 as identifying source items, so a repeated k1 code is the same independent unit entered again, not a new unit.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"`k1` identifies a first-collection source item measured by column `a`; `k2` identifies a second-collection source item measured by column `b`.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow passes every staged row, including the duplicate entries, into an independent-samples t-test, a procedure that treats each row value as an independent observation.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"staged = rows\\nleft = [float(row[\\\"a\\\"]) for row in staged]\\nright = [float(row[\\\"b\\\"]) for row in staged]\\nresult = st.ttest_ind(left, right)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report's degrees of freedom (46.0 = 24+24-2) confirm that all duplicated entries were counted as independent observations; 12 unique units per collection would yield df=22.\", \"observed_value\": \"df=46.0\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-0.9823619317924353), pvalue=np.float64(0.33106037814548595), df=np.float64(46.0))\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The task explicitly instructs applying the procedure to the complete staged row sequence, so processing the duplicates was authorized instruction-following; this bears on fault attribution but does not negate that the repeated-unit entries are demonstrably present in the computed result.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Apply the named procedure to the complete staged row sequence.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to falsify by hypothesizing that the paired lines are distinct units or distinct repeat measurements that would not constitute the same unit re-entering. This fails: the task defines k1/k2 as unit identifiers, and the duplicated rows carry identical identifiers, so they are the same units by the governing definition; even if read as second measurements, the same unit still enters the row-independent procedure twice. I also checked whether the procedure might account for repetition; ttest_ind has no such mechanism, and df=46.0 confirms all 48 values were counted.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:cd04c7b6e14ed2565d4c\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"All 12 k1 identifiers (u01–u12) and all 12 k2 identifiers are distinct, so each source item enters the procedure exactly once.\", \"observed_value\": \"12 rows, no repeated identifier\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 2, \"quoted_text\": \"u01,v07,shared,1.0,2.0\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 13, \"quoted_text\": \"u12,v06,shared,12.0,12.0\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report's df=22.0 (12+12-2) confirms each unit contributed a single observation to the independent-samples t-test.\", \"observed_value\": \"df=22.0\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-0.6793662204867575), pvalue=np.float64(0.5039915691282064), df=np.float64(22.0))\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Every row carries the identical tag value 'shared', which could be read as marking a common cluster; however the task declares tag an opaque annotation, and a shared annotation is not a repeated entry of the same identified source item.\", \"observed_value\": \"tag='shared' on all 12 rows\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 2, \"quoted_text\": \"u01,v07,shared,1.0,2.0\"}, {\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"`tag` is an opaque annotation.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to falsify the negative verdict by treating the uniform 'shared' tag as evidence that the rows are repeated entries of one underlying unit or cluster. This reading is not supported by the visible files: the governing task defines units via k1/k2, which are all distinct, and explicitly designates tag as opaque. No unit identifier repeats and df=22 matches 12 unique units per collection, so repeated-unit entry is not demonstrated.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:e6a9626c34de8381179f\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"All 12 k1 identifiers (u01–u12) and all 12 k2 identifiers are distinct, so each source item enters the procedure exactly once.\", \"observed_value\": \"12 rows, no repeated identifier\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 2, \"quoted_text\": \"u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 13, \"quoted_text\": \"u12,v06,t12,12.0,12.0\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The independent-samples t-test with df=22.0 (12+12-2) matches the stated structure of two disjoint collections with one entry per unit, and the task states the row pairing carries no relationship, so an unpaired test is consistent with the visible task.\", \"observed_value\": \"df=22.0\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-0.6793662204867575), pvalue=np.float64(0.5039915691282064), df=np.float64(22.0))\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The only candidate for the issue is that both samples are extracted from the same staged rows; however the task declares the row pairing a storage convention with no relationship, and no k1 or k2 identifier appears more than once, so no unit enters repeatedly.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 6, \"end_line\": 7, \"quoted_text\": \"left = [float(row[\\\"a\\\"]) for row in staged]\\nright = [float(row[\\\"b\\\"]) for row in staged]\"}, {\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"The row pairing is a storage convention only; there is no matching, pairing, block, or other relationship between the `k1` item and the `k2` item in that row.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to falsify the negative verdict by scanning all rows for any repeated k1 code, repeated k2 code, or duplicated row, and by checking whether the reported degrees of freedom imply more observations than unique units. All identifiers are distinct and df=22.0 matches exactly one observation per unit per collection. No basis for demonstrating repeated unit entry was found.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:e85a81f14d3f395b2b66\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"All 12 k1 identifiers and all 12 k2 identifiers are distinct, so no source item enters the analysis more than once; the precondition of repeated unit entry is absent.\", \"observed_value\": \"12 rows, no repeated identifier\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 2, \"quoted_text\": \"u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 13, \"quoted_text\": \"u12,v06,t12,12.0,12.0\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The applied procedure is a paired (row-dependent) t-test, not a row-independent procedure, so the in-scope issue class — repeated entry into a row-independent procedure — cannot be instantiated by this workflow regardless of the data.\", \"observed_value\": \"ttest_rel, df=11\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"result = st.ttest_rel(left, right)\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-3.63318042491699), pvalue=np.float64(0.00393470596182021), df=np.int64(11))\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The report reflects a serious methodological problem — a paired test was applied although the task states the row pairing carries no relationship — but that is fabrication of dependence via an inappropriate row-dependent procedure, a different concern that is outside this review's issue class and must not be recorded as it.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"The row pairing is a storage convention only; there is no matching, pairing, block, or other relationship between the `k1` item and the `k2` item in that row.\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"result = st.ttest_rel(left, right)\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to falsify the negative verdict two ways: (1) searching for any repeated k1/k2 identifier or duplicated row — none exist; (2) considering whether the paired-test misuse could be recast as the in-scope class — it cannot, because ttest_rel is a row-dependent procedure and no unit enters more than once, whereas the in-scope class requires repeated unit entries into a row-independent procedure. The visible defect is real but belongs to a different issue class.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:f5df454bf6b8da3d72c8\", \"verdict\": \"conditional_or_unknown\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Each k1 code appears exactly twice with different measurement values (e.g., u01 with a=1.0 and a=2.0, through u06 with a=11.0 and a=12.0), so if k1 codes identified source items, each first-collection unit would enter the a-sample twice.\", \"observed_value\": \"6 distinct k1 codes over 12 rows, each appearing twice\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 3, \"quoted_text\": \"u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0\\nu01,v11,t02,2.0,4.0\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 12, \"end_line\": 13, \"quoted_text\": \"u06,v08,t11,11.0,13.0\\nu06,v02,t12,12.0,12.0\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow enters all 12 a-values into an independent-samples t-test, which treats them as 12 independent observations (df=22.0), so the procedure is row-independent and would be affected if the repeated codes denote repeated units.\", \"observed_value\": \"df=22.0\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] TtestResult(statistic=np.float64(-0.6793662204867575), pvalue=np.float64(0.5039915691282064), df=np.float64(22.0))\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Unlike a definition that binds codes to units, this task explicitly declares k1 and k2 opaque and states that it does not establish whether either code identifies a source item, so the repeated k1 codes cannot be shown from the visible files to be repeated entries of the same unit.\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Treat `k1` and `k2` as opaque codes; `tag` is an opaque annotation. This task does not establish whether either code identifies a source item within either collection.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to resolve the verdict in both directions. Toward 'demonstrated': the doubled k1 codes with distinct a-values strongly resemble repeated measurements of six units entering a row-independent test, but the governing task explicitly withholds the code-to-unit mapping, so asserting the issue would require guessing unstated semantics, which the review protocol forbids. Toward 'no demonstrated issue': the same withheld mapping also prevents me from ruling the issue out, because if u-codes do identify units the report demonstrably double-counts each of six units. The determination is blocked by a fact the visible files deliberately leave open, so neither definitive verdict is supportable.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [\"Does a repeated k1 code (each of u01–u06 appears on exactly two rows) denote the same first-collection source item, such that its two a-values are repeated entries of one independent unit into the independent-samples t-test?\"], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"medium\"}]}","ttft_ms":75100,"ttft_stream_ms":3276,"time_to_request_ms":527,"type":"result","duration_ms":141864,"uuid":"b5cded62-4539-45c4-8131-1a6c211da622"}
